id: pm-csv-sdk-adoption-1025
title: Use the pm SDK for runtime CSV export fields
description: "Resolve audit findings with SDK settings and runtime field registry; evaluate native mutation and fenced update adoption against the supported host floor. Preserve verified history, prove real public tracker export equivalence, and record per-finding revert evidence. Related adoption: pm-csv-axm5; persistence prerequisite: pm-csv-sdk-write-fence."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T16:45:54.747Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T03:14:09.462Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-26T03:14:06.928Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T17:26:15.000Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: "Delivered by PR #196, merge ec5b50f55e68a6b4be95ef50640fdfe158f8273c, merged 2026-10-25T17:26:15Z. index.ts discoverCustomFields awaits readSettingsWithMetadata and resolves canonical runtime definitions with resolveRuntimeFieldRegistry on both export surfaces. test/sdk-adoption.test.ts covers schema normalization, file precedence, no-git preservation and corrupted-history refusal. The item requires evaluating native mutation adoption; its documented evaluation retains atomic-update.ts and roundtrip.ts until the separately tracked SDK guarantees exist."
expected_result: "Runtime CSV export field discovery uses SDK settings/registry, preserves tested export contracts and explicitly evaluates safety prerequisites."
actual_result: "Four focused adoption regressions pass on main. The field-discovery replacement and evaluation are delivered; pm-csv-sdk-write-fence remains open under PR #198, and no atomic mutation migration is claimed."
